.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt WAITPID 2
.Os Project9
.Sh NAME
.Nm waitpid ,
.Nm exitstatus
.Nd collect child status or exit with a status code
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In types.h
.In user.h
.In wait.h
.Ft int
.Fn waitpid "int pid" "int *status" "int options"
.Ft void
.Fn exitstatus "int status"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn waitpid
collects a child event.
A positive PID selects one child, zero the caller's process group,
-1 any child and a value below -1 the group with that absolute ID.
The default reports exit or termination.
.Dv WUNTRACED
also reports a stop, and
.Dv WCONTINUED
reports resumption.
.Dv WNOHANG
returns immediately when there is a matching child with no reportable
event.
Use the macros in
.In wait.h
to interpret the status word.
The status pointer can be null.
.Fn exitstatus
ends the caller and records the low eight bits of its argument.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn waitpid
returns the child PID on an event, zero for a nonblocking wait with no
event, or -1 if the request is invalid, interrupted or has no matching
child.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr send_signal 2
